The factors considered were as follows:
"(i) Whether the offence affects society at large;
(ii) The likelihood of the crime being repeated;
(iii) The potential of the convict to commit crimes in the future;
(iv) Whether any meaningful purpose is served by keeping the convict in prison; and (v) The socio-economic condition of the convict's family."
